{"name":"Bioluminescence","hex":"#55eeff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bioluminescence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The emission of light by a living organism (such as a firefly)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bioluminescence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bioluminescence","blocks":[{"text":"Bioluminescence is the production of light by an organism as the result of a chemiluminescence reaction. It occurs in a wide variety of organisms, including marine vertebrates and invertebrates, terrestrial arthropods such as fireflies, some fungi, and microorganisms such as some bacteria and dinoflagellates. In some animals, the light is bacteriogenic, produced by symbiotic bacteria such as those from the genus Vibrio; in others, it is autogenic, produced by the animals themselves. Bioluminescence has evolved independently at least 94 times, first emerging in octocorals some 540 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Photinus_pyralis_Firefly_glowing.jpg/330px-Photinus_pyralis_Firefly_glowing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioluminescence","wikidata":"Q179924"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg/330px-Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg/330px-Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female glowworm, Lampyris noctiluca","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALampyris_noctiluca.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Aequorea4.jpg/500px-Aequorea4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Aequorea4.jpg/500px-Aequorea4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Osamu Shimomura isolated the photoprotein aequorin and its cofactor coelenterazine from the crystal jelly Aequorea victoria in 1961.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAequorea4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png/500px-Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png/500px-Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Protein structure of the luciferase of the firefly Photinus pyralis. The enzyme is a much larger molecule than luciferin.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/500px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/1280px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/500px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mycena chlorophos, a bioluminescent mushroom. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMycena_chlorophos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Squid_Counterillumination.png/500px-Squid_Counterillumination.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Squid_Counterillumination.png/500px-Squid_Cou